# Logging (S3-10)

Every API route handler and Server Action in Solution Wizard V2 must go
through the shared logging/audit infrastructure in `lib/`. This exists so a
demo or production incident can be traced end-to-end from a single
`traceId`, without ever leaking secrets into logs. Background:
`docs/2026-08-logging/technical-task-logging.md`.

## Required for every `app/api/**/route.ts` handler

- Wrap the exported handler (`GET`/`POST`/`PATCH`/...) with
  `withLogging("<event-name>", handler)` from `lib/with-logging.ts`. Do not
  call `console.log`/`console.error` directly — use `logger` from
  `lib/logger.ts` (or let `withLogging` handle it for you on
  success/error/thrown exceptions).
- Pick an `event` name in `<resource>.<verb>` form, matching the existing
  ones (`blueprint.patch`, `bpmn.sync`, `chat.post`, `poc.generate`, ...).
- If the route performs a security-relevant or data-changing action
  (auth, session creation, blueprint/BPMN mutation, PoC generation), call
  `audit(event, { actor, resource, outcome, ... })` from `lib/audit.ts` for
  both the success and the denied/error paths. See the `AuditEvent` union in
  `lib/audit.ts` for the allowed event names — add a new one there rather
  than inventing an ad-hoc string.

## Required for every Server Action (`app/**/actions.ts`)

- Server Actions don't run through `withLogging`'s `AsyncLocalStorage`
  scope, so read the trace id via `getIncomingTraceId()` from
  `lib/request-context.ts` (it falls back to a fresh id outside a request
  scope, e.g. in tests) rather than assuming one is set.
- Auth-affecting actions (`login`, `devSignIn`, `signOut`) must call `audit()`
  **before** any `redirect()` call — `redirect()` throws, so anything after
  it never runs.

## Never log

- Passwords, tokens, cookies, or API keys, even redacted forms should not be
  attempted manually — `lib/logger.ts`'s `redact` config already covers the
  known paths; extend that config, don't work around it.
- Full chat message content or full blueprint bodies. Log identifiers,
  counts, and outcomes (e.g. `stepCount`, not the blueprint JSON itself).

## Review checklist

A new or modified route/action that does **not** call `withLogging` (routes)
or `getIncomingTraceId`/`audit` (actions, where applicable) should be flagged
in review and sent back — this is exactly the gap S3-10 closed, don't
reopen it silently by adding an unwrapped route later.
